Synthetic signing fixtures (decision 0009). Nothing in this directory belongs to a funded account.

- The Starknet account address in signbench/main.rs and ParadexHashOracle.java is the example
  account printed in Paradex's public API documentation (the "Get JWT" page), not an owner
  account.
- The private key beside it is a test value chosen for the benchmark. It is not the key of that
  documented account or of any account the owner uses; it exists only so the hash and signature
  vectors are reproducible.
- The chain id is Paradex's public mainnet chain id; the order fields (market, size, price,
  timestamp) are made-up inputs.
- signbench/main.rs also benchmarks other venues' signers with public test values only: the
  secp256k1 keys are the well-known example key from the web3 documentation and the test key
  in the public Java library's GrvtEip712OrderSignerTest, and the Hyperliquid vectors are the
  ones in that venue's public Python SDK tests. None belongs to an owner account.
- The GRVT subAccountID (8289849667772468), nonce and expiry in signbench/main.rs are the
  GRVT Python SDK's test_sign_order_table fixture values, also used in the public Java
  library's GrvtEip712OrderSignerTest; they are not an owner sub-account.
- Every other long hex value here (order hashes, signature r and s, the derived client-id
  hash) is computed from those inputs.

This marker covers fixtures/paradex/signing/ only. Recorded Paradex frames and journals go
elsewhere under fixtures/paradex/, where the privacy check scans them.

These files reproduce the golden vectors the Paradex signer is checked against: the Java
library's hash and signature for the inputs above (ParadexHashOracle.java runs the Java
signer), and the Rust benchmark that recovered the same values (signbench/).
